            <ArticleTitle>[One patient - many faces of myocardial ischaemia].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>631-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.5603/KP.2013.0132</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present the case of a woman treated with coronary angioplasty due to non-ST segment elevation myocardial infarction,then again because of restenosis, who continued to complain of chest pain and syncope. Holter electrocardiogram recording revealed atrioventricular block related to ST-segment elevations and variant angina was diagnosed. Despite administered medications, the patient required pacemaker implantation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
